-- title:
--   Rank of (ℚ⊗ A)/(g(j)) equals (p+1)deg g
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and let $F = \mathbb{Q}(\mathrm{divisorExpansions}\,p)$ be the full modular function field of level $p$: the subfield of the Laurent series field $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,\mathbb{Q}\,d\,j$ for the nonzero divisors $d$ of $p$, and let $j \in F$ denote the expansion of the modular invariant itself (`IgusaScheme.jFull p`). Write $A$ for the finite-chart subalgebra `chartAlg` of $F$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ attached to the one-element set $\{j\}$, denoted `Afin p`, and $j \in A$ for the canonical element `jChartFin` of that subalgebra. The assertion is that for every nonzero $g \in \mathbb{Z}[X]$ the quotient of the $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra $\mathbb{Q} \otimes_{\mathbb{Z}} A$ by the principal ideal generated by $1 \otimes g(j)$, where $g(j)$ is the image of $g$ under evaluation at $j \in A$, has $\mathbb{Q}$-dimension exactly $(p+1)\cdot \deg g$, the degree being the `natDegree` of $g$.
--
--   This is the generic-fibre rank computation for the finite-$j$ chart of the integral model of $X_0(p)$: rationally that chart ring is a free module of rank $[\,F:\mathbb{Q}(j)\,] = [\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z}):\Gamma_0(p)] = p+1$ over $\mathbb{Q}[j]$, so cutting by $g(j)$ leaves a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra of dimension $(p+1)\deg g$. It feeds the construction of finite étale level rings over the chart, via [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_finite_etale_levelRing_jChartFin).
